{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And he who sends… to Azazel.</b> One must know what Azazel is, and our Sages of blessed memory (Yoma 67b) explained it as עַז וְקָשֶׁה — strong and harsh. And there are many derashot on this, but in any case the mind is not reconciled. And my eyes were illumined by the words of the men of truth who delve into the gates of the lights of Torah, who said (Zohar 2:157a) that the wilderness that was barren is the place of Samael the wicked, and accordingly this aspect is called ״מִדְבָּר״ (wilderness), and is called ״עֲזָאזֵל״, and is called ״עוּזָא וַעֲזָאֵל״ — Uza and Azael — as they of blessed memory said that this name alludes to them. And perhaps the word itself declares this in this manner: עַז אָזַל — meaning, the place of those who went (אָזַל) and gathered the strength (עֹז) of their splendor. Or in this manner: עֲזָא זַל — meaning, the place of the power that is זַל, in the language of depreciation and lowliness, for Samael is lower in rank than all the ministering angels above."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:57:37.151613042Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}